      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T16:19:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I\u0027m afraid I drove you the wrong way -- normally the flag would just work automatically, the Zephyr APIs return a logical value, but now that I\u0027ve checked, `button.c` uses `gpio_get_level`, which is implemented using `gpio_pin_get_raw`, which is the same as `gpio_pin_get` but bypasses the `ACTIVE_LOW` bit.\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/gpio.c;l\u003d106\nhttps://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/include/zephyr/drivers/gpio.h#L1475-L1477\n\napologies for throwing you off, so either add back those config or add a Zephyr specific implementation of `raw_button_pressed` (there\u0027s few different code path in common, look for `CONFIG_ZEPHYR`). Up to you I guess.",
      "parentUuid": "a9b901a8_6ec4f39a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 341,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "00603e97bf5757cc1ec7a6465abfc18afe9773aa",
